concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-3-sec-2-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2(3) Subsections 45(1) to (3)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-2-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) For the purposes of this section, competition means:  (a) in relation to a provision of a contract, arrangement or understanding or of a proposed contract, arrangement or understanding—competition in any market in which:  (i) a corporation that is a party to the contract, arrangement or understanding, or would be a party to the proposed contract, arrangement or understanding; or  Price signalling and concerted practices  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 114, 2017 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review) Act 2017  (ii) any body corporate related to such a corporation;  supplies or acquires, or is likely to supply or acquire, goods or services or would, but for the provision, supply or acquire, or be likely to supply or acquire, goods or services; or  (b) in relation to a concerted practice—competition in any market in which:  (i) a corporation that is a party to the practice; or  (ii) any body corporate related to such a corporation;  supplies or acquires, or is likely to supply or acquire, goods or services or would, but for the practice, supply or acquire, or be likely to supply or acquire, goods or services." ;
    skos:definition "(3) For the purposes of this section, competition means:  (a) in relation to a provision of a contract, arrangement or understanding or of a proposed contract, arrangement or understanding—competition in any market in which:  (i) a corporation that is a party to the contract, arrangement or understanding, or would be a party to the proposed contract, arrangement or understanding; or  Price signalling and concerted practices  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 114, 2017 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Competition Policy Review) Act 2017  (ii) any body corporate related to such a corporation;  supplies or acquires, or is likely to supply or acquire, goods or services or would, but for the provision, supply or acquire, or be likely to supply or acquire, goods or services; or  (b) in relation to a concerted practice—competition in any market in which:  (i) a corporation that is a party to the practice; or  (ii) any body corporate related to such a corporation;  supplies or acquires, or is likely to supply or acquire, goods or services or would, but for the practice, supply or acquire, or be likely to supply or acquire, goods or services."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cbcac001ae0090ca9939eb33ac47ac78a908eba76b96cf12209d1ded2615ec22" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-3-sec-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines competition in relation to a provision of a contract, arrangement or understanding." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017.pdf> ;
