concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-competition-policy-review-act-2017-sch-9-sec-29 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29 Subsection 4(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-9-sec-29 ;
    values:originalText "Insert: collective boycott conduct means conduct that has a purpose referred to in subsection 44ZZRD(3) in relation to a contract, arrangement or understanding. merger authorisation means an authorisation that:  (a) is an authorisation for a person to engage in conduct to which section 50 or 50A would or might apply; but  (b) is not an authorisation for a person to engage in conduct to which any provision of Part IV other than section 50 or 50A would or might apply. overseas merger authorisation means a merger authorisation that is not an authorisation for a person to engage in conduct to which section 50 would or might apply." ;
    skos:definition "Insert: collective boycott conduct means conduct that has a purpose referred to in subsection 44ZZRD(3) in relation to a contract, arrangement or understanding. merger authorisation means an authorisation that:  (a) is an authorisation for a person to engage in conduct to which section 50 or 50A would or might apply; but  (b) is not an authorisation for a person to engage in conduct to which any provision of Part IV other than section 50 or 50A would or might apply. overseas merger authorisation means a merger authorisation that is not an authorisation for a person to engage in conduct to which section 50 would or might apply."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ddcfba1f85ec8d0fff745e4d3381a4da85b6fd5740473319b3bc5a32bb8962f7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "57"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines collective boycott conduct and merger authorisation." ;
